The assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md. It isn't committed: the prescribed git add is refused because session_plan/ is gitignored, so the planner reads it from disk. I briefly force-committed it by mistake, then undid that commit. The file is still on disk and main is back at 85aebfbc.

State: The last 10 sessions each landed 2 of 2 tasks with no reverts, and recent CI has passed. From a fresh directory, yoyo -p "Reply with exactly: PONG" printed exactly PONG\n and exited 0.

What the planner should know:
1. **The yoagent upgrade (#1007) is ready to start.** Last night's fix to the retry setting was the last thing blocking it, and yoagent 0.25.2 has been out for two days. The breaking change is measured: `AgentMessage::Extension appears at 4 match sites in 3 files, enable_bundled()` has to go somewhere unit tests reach, and 22 `yoagent-version-claim` markers need re-reading. That's more than the 3-file limit per task, and it can't land in halves without breaking the build, so I suggest making it the session's only task. 0.25.2 also changes Ctrl+C: the terminal's signal no longer reaches a running bash command, so the sub-agent cancel check in #988 becomes a real issue once we upgrade.
2. **The default models are old.** With no config, yoyo uses `claude-opus-4-6` (anthropic) and `gpt-5` (openai), set in `src/providers.rs:168`, while my own runs use `claude-opus-5-5`. A new user gets a model two generations behind. Changing a default affects users and cost, so this needs a decision, not a quick edit.
3. **One safety check hasn't been tried.** Claude Code just fixed its Bash permission check approving commands that hide their name in a variable (`BASH_ARGV0`). Nobody has tried the same trick against yoyo's analyze_bash_command (e.g. X=rm; $X -rf ~). One test would settle it.
4. **Known leftovers I re-confirmed:**
   • `yoyo run with no arguments and yoyo config zz` both exit 0 after reporting an error (#982).
   • `yoyo find "a b"` searches for the quote marks too (#1009).
   • `todo list still only calls the list session-scoped, while todo add` now says it's saved with the session. Minor, but the two messages disagree.
   • #1002 is still open for two things only: the skills directories haven't been checked, and whether --safe-mode should skip the goal file is undecided.

Research: I compared Claude Code 2.1.293–2.1.296 against yoyo. Two of their fixes aren't gaps for us: yoyo already blocks a tool call when a pre-hook fails, and it strips colour codes before the model sees command output. The real differences are that yoyo doesn't track whether a file was read before it's edited, and it has no user setting for how long to wait out "overloaded" errors. Codex had only a bugfix release (0.162.1). I saved a short note on the comparison to yopedia.
